---
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import { REPOSITORY, components, url } from "../../lib/data";

const toc = [
  { id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works" },
  { id: "what-is-included", label: "What is included" },
  { id: "live-previews", label: "Live previews" },
];

const example = `use shadcn_iced::prelude::*;

fn view(_state: &()) -> iced::Element<'_, Message> {
    card()
        .title("Create project")
        .description("Deploy your new project in one-click.")
        .footer(button("Deploy").on_press(Message::Save))
        .width(350)
        .into()
}`;
---

<Docs
  title="Introduction"
  description="Beautifully designed components for iced, ported from shadcn/ui. Use them as a library, or copy them into your project and make them your own."
  toc={toc}
  next={{ href: url("/docs/installation"), label: "Installation" }}
>
  <p>
    shadcn-iced brings the components of <a href="https://ui.shadcn.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">shadcn/ui</a>
    to <a href="https://iced.rs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">iced</a>, the cross-platform GUI library for Rust.
    It follows the current default style of shadcn/ui (Base UI with the Nova style), down to its spacing, colors,
    radii and animations.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock class="mt-6" code={example} title="src/main.rs" />

  <h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>
  <p>Like shadcn/ui, shadcn-iced is the code of its components first. You choose how to use it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>As a library</strong>: depend on the <code>shadcn_iced</code> crate and update it like any dependency.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Copy and paste</strong>: <code>cargo shadcn-iced add button dialog</code> writes the source of the components to
      <code>src/ui/</code>, where you can change anything.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Both share <code>shadcn_iced_core</code>: the theme, the fonts and icons, and the headless primitives (anchored
    overlays, modal layers, listboxes, disclosures) that Base UI provides to shadcn/ui.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-is-included">What is included</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={url("/docs/components")}>{components.length} components</a>, the whole registry of shadcn/ui.</li>
    <li>
      Every theme of the <code>/create</code> page of shadcn/ui: 7 base colors, 17 themes, chart colors, radii and
      menu styles, in light and dark mode. See <a href={url("/docs/theming")}>Theming</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Geist, Geist Mono and Inter, and all 2,179 Lucide icons, bundled.</li>
    <li>The animations of tw-animate-css for overlays, sheets, accordions and toasts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="live-previews">Live previews</h2>
  <p>
    The previews of this site are not screenshots. Each one runs the example from the
    <a href={`${REPOSITORY}/tree/main/examples/gallery`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">gallery</a>
    with iced compiled to WebAssembly, drawn with WebGPU (or a software renderer when your browser lacks it). The
    Code tab shows the source that builds it. Use the Theme menu in the header to see them in any theme.
  </p>
</Docs>
